<Base title="About — Sebastián Ortiz de Zevallos" currentPage="about">
  <article class="project">
    <h1 class="project__title">About</h1>

    <div class="project__body">
      <p>
        Sebastián Ortiz de Zevallos is a Peruvian architect, urbanist, and
        computational designer based in Madrid. He works independently across
        parametric architecture, computational geometry, and audiovisual
        practice.
      </p>

      <p>
        Trained at the Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú (PUCP) and the
        Institute for Advanced Architecture of Catalonia (IAAC), his work
        operates at the intersection of algorithmic design, sound analysis, and
        spatial research.
      </p>

      <p>
        Recent projects include parametric facade systems driven by attractor
        curves, audio-reactive installations using stem separation and pitch
        extraction pipelines, and the audiovisual exhibition <em
          >Secciones de Sonido — un experimento en tres tiempos</em
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Tools</h2>
      <p>
        Rhinoceros, Grasshopper, Anemone, Python, C#, Blender, Touch Designer,
        DaVinci Resolve, custom audio analysis pipelines (librosa, Demucs).
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Selected studies</h2>
      <p>
        M.Adv.S. — IAAC, Barcelona<br />
        Architecture — PUCP, Lima
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
